                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Lots of variety with bosses and enemies. Includes interesting time-based events mid-mission and enemies that come from all four directions, which gets pretty exciting pretty quickly.  Well done, A To Play Ltd's Flight of the Athena is pretty damn fun and very replayable!\n\nWhile the portrait art may be lacking the rest of the in-game art are quite nice. Some odd design decisions on the tactical map but the actual battles and bosses are loads of fun. And multiplayer!\n\nFor more niche curation, follow me at: https://store.steampowered.com/curator/27440015-CSH-Picone/",
